# Formatting for Arches Instrumentation (REQ §14: consistent style, no drift).
#
# Microsoft style (Allman braces, which is what this tree is actually written
# in) with a deliberately very wide column limit, tuned to the house
# conventions so a finding means real drift rather than a fight over idiom:
#   - ColumnLimit 300 is effectively "do not re-wrap". Lines here are broken
#     where the author judged the break to read best -- long gRPC signatures,
#     descriptor tables and REQ-referencing comments all suffer from mechanical
#     wrapping. 300 is not a target width; nothing in the tree approaches it.
#     It is the way to say "leave my line breaks alone" in a clang-format
#     config, since there is no setting that means exactly that.
#   - One-liners stay one-liners where clang-format allows it: short case
#     labels (`case X: return "y";` name maps), braceless short ifs/loops,
#     single-statement and empty blocks (`} catch (...) {}`). Multi-statement
#     blocks are still split -- clang-format has no setting to keep those.
#   - Comments are hand-wrapped and hand-aligned (doxygen file headers, REQ
#     §-references, struct field comments). ReflowComments is off so the text
#     is never re-flowed, and AlignTrailingComments is `Leave` so the existing
#     column alignment is preserved exactly as written.
#
#     `Leave` matters and is not the same as `false`: `false` means "do not
#     align", which makes clang-format actively collapse hand-aligned padding
#     down to a single space. This file used to say `false` while its own
#     comment promised that clang-format "never moves them", and the result
#     was that `make check-format` failed on 26 untouched files across the
#     tree. See Task.md G-01.
#   - Includes are left exactly as written (SortIncludes: Never): the house
#     order -- main header, blank line, system block, blank line, project
#     block -- is deliberate, and Google's block regrouping would churn it.
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Microsoft
ColumnLimit: 300
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: WithoutElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortLambdasOnASingleLine: All
AlignTrailingComments:
  Kind: Leave
  OverEmptyLines: 0
ReflowComments: false
SortIncludes: Never
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
